                <pb facs="0152" n="58" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg58"/>

                <head>No. 52.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Trail</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 25,
                        1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 51.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In view of a communication of the 21st
                    instant from Mr. E. R. Bacon, of the American Telegraph and Cable Company, you
                    were telegraphed on the 23d instant as follows: “Use good offices for extending
                    concessions to Pedro Segundo American Cable Company.”</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">T. F. Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
